@* The split button: a default action, and a menu of the others. The two are separate buttons, so
   the common case is one click and the menu never gets in its way.

   The trigger has to be a DIRECT child of the group. The joins are made by `[&>*]` selectors, so
   wrapping the trigger in <DropdownMenu> put a plain div in the group's child list: the div lost
   its radius, the button inside kept all four corners, and the split showed a rounded button
   floating inside a squared-off slot. <DropdownMenu> is only a positioning anchor — leave it
   out and the trigger is the child. *@
<ButtonGroup>
    <Button Variant="secondary">Publish</Button>
    <ButtonGroupSeparator />
    <DropdownMenuTrigger Target="bg-split" Variant="secondary" Size="icon"
                         aria-label="More publish options">
        <Icon Name="chevron-down" />
    </DropdownMenuTrigger>
</ButtonGroup>

<DropdownMenuContent Id="bg-split" Align="end" Class="w-48">
    <DropdownMenuItem>Publish and notify</DropdownMenuItem>
    <DropdownMenuItem>Schedule…</DropdownMenuItem>
    <DropdownMenuSeparator />
    <DropdownMenuItem>Save as a draft</DropdownMenuItem>
</DropdownMenuContent>
